    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d129">

                <pb facs="0245" n="127" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg127"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">314.115C43/45</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Guatemala</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Geissler</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Guatemala</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1928-07-16">July 16, 1928</date>.<lb/>[Received July
                        25.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 2019</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit a copy of a
                    letter in which Mr. P. W. Shufeldt, under date of July 6<anchor n="7"
                        xml:id="d129-f1"/> expresses a desire for action on the part of the
                    President of Guatemala in the matter of the Bill passed by the Legislative
                    Assembly, regarding his chicle concession; and also a copy of my answer of July
                        14,<anchor n="8" xml:id="d129-f2"/> informing him, that, according to <hi
                        rendition="#italic">El Guatemalteco</hi>, the Bill was signed by the
                    President on July 4, and that, on July 10, I had inquired of the Minister for
                    Foreign Affairs whether a rumored plan of the Government to dispossess him
                    through issuing licenses to other parties would be legal <pb facs="0246" n="128"
                        xml:id="pg128"/> and constitutional, and that the Minister, without
                    committing himself to me regarding that point, had remarked that he had hoped
                    that a mutually satisfactory arrangement would be effected between Mr. Shufeldt
                    and the Minister of Agriculture.</p>
                <p>It appears, that the Act as signed conforms to the Legislative Bill, as
                    translated on page two of despatch No. 1938 of May 22, 1928,<anchor n="9"
                        xml:id="d129-f3"/> with the exception of some immaterial variations.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Arthur H.
                    Geissler</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
